From rekow at bigskytel.com  Fri May 28 18:15:08 2004
From: rekow at bigskytel.com (Buck Rekow)
Date: Fri, 28 May 2004 12:15:08 -0600
Subject: SRM help? (fwd)
References: <1085766927.24800.TMDA@mail.js1.bogus>
Message-ID: <40B781AC.4020002@bigskytel.com>

I know it'scalled autoboot, and you set it like an environment variable. 
if your SRM is new enough you will have help on the subject. I don't 
know if you can interrupt SRM, but you can force the boot to fail, which 
will drop you to SRM. pull your primary boot disk, and boot.. the boot 
will fail and SRM will appear. check out the help on autoboot.




From marco at xssnet.com  Fri May 28 18:22:04 2004
From: marco at xssnet.com (Marco Benton)
Date: Fri, 28 May 2004 14:22:04 -0400
Subject: SRM help? (fwd)
